EVENT (live today, Berlin): GTM Hackathon "Detect the signal. Build the agent." Build 11:00–17:30 (~6h), live demo required.
TRACKS (each has a prize): Apify "Capture" — find a signal nobody is using ($250 Apify credits/member). n8n "Act" — close the loop, no human in the middle (n8n Cloud Pro/member). Featherless "Out of the box" — the unexpected data source that works ($300 credits/team). Grand prize across all tracks.
JUDGING: 1 Originality — how fresh is the signal? 2 Real solution — runs today, usable on Monday. 3 Reliability — fails gracefully, holds up under GDPR. 4 Wild card — the idea, the craft, the ambition. Organizer quote: "A small thing that runs beats a big thing that does not."
NEW INPUT FROM THE ORGANIZERS' TALK: the key factor for GTM signals is ROI. Clay and standard companies already use the obvious signals: hiring signals, funding signals ("they just raised, they need to spend money"), marketing problems. So an original signal must beat these on freshness/predictiveness AND show ROI.
Bella&Bona (office-lunch + catering, Berlin/Munich, opened NRW Düsseldorf/Köln on 1 Oct 2026, sells a tax-free meal benefit €7.67/workday, claims "30–40% higher office attendance", buyers = People Ops) is only a host providing lunch, NOT a track sponsor. German UWG §7: no unsolicited B2B email automation.

